.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-key-generate 1  "tapectl-key-generate " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-key\-generate \- Generate a new keypair for a tenant, or the permanent escrow recipient with \-\-escrow (ADR\-0005)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl key generate\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\fR] [\fB\-\-alias\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-type\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-escrow\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate a new keypair for a tenant, or the permanent escrow recipient with \-\-escrow (ADR\-0005)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR \fI<TENANT>\fR
Tenant name (required unless \-\-escrow)
.TP
\fB\-\-alias\fR \fI<ALIAS>\fR
Key alias (e.g., "primary", "backup", "2026") (required unless \-\-escrow)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-type\fR \fI<KEY_TYPE>\fR [default: primary]
Key type
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
Description
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file
.TP
\fB\-\-escrow\fR
Generate the permanent escrow recipient identity instead of a per\-tenant key (ADR\-0005). Prints the secret exactly once, for paper transcription — tapectl never stores it. Refuses if an escrow identity is already registered; there is only ever one, for the life of the archive
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
